.TH METEOSERVER 1 "November 2026" "meteo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
meteoserver \- websocket server for a Vaisala weather station
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B meteoserver
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a Vaisala MAWS weather station over a serial port and a GPS receiver
through gpsd, and pushes the data to web clients via websocket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-ip\fR=\fIIP\fR
Listen IP address or host [default: all interfaces]
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR=\fIport\fR
Listen port [default: 8080]
.TP
\fB\-\-serial\fR=\fIdevice\fR
Serial device [default: /dev/ttyUSB0]
.TP
\fB\-\-baudrate\fR=\fIbaudrate\fR
Serial baudrate [default: 9600]
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR=\fIid\fR
Websocket group id [default: \-1]
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR=\fIid\fR
Websocket user id [default: \-1]
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-daemon\fR
Run meteoserver as a daemon
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR=\fIlevel\fR
libwebsockets log level bitmask [default: 7 (errors, warnings, notices)]
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gps\fR
Disable GPS support
.TP
\fB\-?\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Give a help list
.TP
\fB\-\-usage\fR
Give a short usage message
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print program version
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/meteo
Options passed by the systemd service (\fBSERVER_OPTIONS\fR).
.TP
.I /var/meteodata
Recorded CSV data.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs to Michael Wolf <michael@mictronics.de>.
.SH AUTHOR
Michael Wolf
